% Mechanical In-exsufflation Devices: LCD L33795 and its Policy Article
% A52510 (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes
% dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills)
% and states when a claim for a mechanical in-exsufflation device (E0482)
% or a replacement interface (A7020) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: a
% neuromuscular disease of the Policy Article's ICD-10 list, causing a
% significant impairment of chest wall or diaphragmatic movement such that
% the beneficiary cannot clear retained secretions. The payment condition
% the Article adds: a replacement interface is paid only for a device the
% beneficiary owns or is purchasing.
%
% How the criteria are read. The neuromuscular disease is the claim's
% diagnosis code (the shared template "the diagnosis code of B is C"), read
% against the Article's ICD-10 table (sources/icd10/A52510_icd10_covered.csv,
% one group, serving E0482 and A7020), loaded as the table mie_icd10 — the
% Article requires the code that justifies the need on the claim, and the
% LCD refers to the Article's list for the diagnoses. The impairment is one
% clinical judgment, the judged template of dmepos.le "the finding F about
% B is established" (or unsupported), with who found it and why:
%   neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance (criterion 2: the
%   condition is causing a significant impairment of chest wall and/or
%   diaphragmatic movement, such that it results in an inability to clear
%   retained secretions).
% That the beneficiary owns or is purchasing the device is a fact of the
% record, "the device is owned by the beneficiary" (a purchase in progress
% counts, as the Article says).
%
% Not modelled: the coding guideline that A7020 must not be billed at
% initial issue (a matter of coding).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a device* is owned by the beneficiary; undefined.   % candidate for dmepos.le
    % the table
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table mie_icd10.
    % derived
    *an item* is a mechanical in-exsufflation device.
    *an item* is a replacement interface for a mechanical in-exsufflation device.
    *a beneficiary* meets the mechanical in-exsufflation coverage criteria.
    *a beneficiary* has a neuromuscular disease listed for mechanical in-exsufflation.
    the neuromuscular disease of *a beneficiary* prevents the clearing of retained secretions.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the covered codes of its one group.
the table mie_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52510_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base mechanical_insufflation includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base mechanical_insufflation includes:

LCD L33795 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33795".
the text of LCD L33795 is at "sources/lcd/L33795.txt".
Policy Article A52510 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52510".
the text of Policy Article A52510 is at "sources/article/A52510.txt".

% What the device and the replacement interface are.
rule mie_device with provenance LCD L33795,
        confer "Mechanical in-exsufflation devices (E0482) are covered for beneficiaries who meet all of the following criteria":
an item is a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0482".

rule mie_interface with provenance Policy Article A52510,
        confer "HCPCS code A7020 (INTERFACE FOR COUGH STIMULATING DEVICE, INCLUDES ALL COMPONENTS, REPLACEMENT ONLY) is for replacement only":
an item is a replacement interface for a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "A7020".

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical
% equipment (Policy Article A52510).
rule mie_codes with provenance Policy Article A52510,
        confer "Mechanical in-exsufflation equipment is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is mechanical_insufflation
    if the code is in ["E0482", "A7020"].

rule mie_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52510,
        confer "Mechanical in-exsufflation equipment is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is mechanical_insufflation.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The device: both criteria. The replacement interface: reasonable and
% necessary when the device it serves is.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule mie_covered with provenance LCD L33795,
        confer "Mechanical in-exsufflation devices (E0482) are covered for beneficiaries who meet all of the following criteria":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the mechanical in-exsufflation coverage criteria.

% the interface follows the device it replaces a part of: a device of this
% model (the LCD states no criterion for A7020)
rule mie_interface_covered:
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a replacement interface for a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the mechanical in-exsufflation coverage criteria.

rule mie_criteria with provenance LCD L33795,
        confer "If both of these criteria are not met, the claim will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a beneficiary meets the mechanical in-exsufflation coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary has a neuromuscular disease listed for mechanical in-exsufflation
    and the neuromuscular disease of the beneficiary prevents the clearing of retained secretions.

% Criterion 1: the diagnosis, a code of the Article's list.
rule mie_criterion_1 with provenance LCD L33795,
        confer "They have a neuromuscular disease (refer to the ICD-10 code list in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
a beneficiary has a neuromuscular disease listed for mechanical in-exsufflation
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52510" as a description under table mie_icd10.

% Criterion 2: the finding.
rule mie_criterion_2 with provenance LCD L33795,
        confer "This condition is causing a significant impairment of chest wall and/or diaphragmatic movement, such that it results in an inability to clear retained secretions":
the neuromuscular disease of a beneficiary prevents the clearing of retained secretions
    if the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about the beneficiary is established.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own condition of payment: a replacement interface
% only for a device the beneficiary owns or is purchasing. The diagnosis
% code the Article requires on the claim is what criterion 1 reads.
rule mie_interface_ownership with provenance Policy Article A52510,
        confer "Reimbursement may be made for replacement of A7020 (INTERFACE FOR COUGH STIMULATING DEVICE, INCLUDES ALL COMPONENTS, REPLACEMENT ONLY) only if the beneficiary owns or is purchasing the mechanical in-exsufflation device":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is mechanical_insufflation
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is a replacement interface for a mechanical in-exsufflation device
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is owned by the beneficiary.

rule mie_device_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52510,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is mechanical_insufflation
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is a mechanical in-exsufflation device.
